{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937113-origin-of-the-god-machine","id":937113,"title":"Origin of the God-Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-25T08:52:08-07:00","id":937113,"title":"Origin of the God-Machine","content":"I am looking for the origin of the God-Machine. The idea I came up with is that the God-Machine was built by the Exarchs to maintain the status quo in the Fallen World (or whatever Earth was called before the Fall) while the Exarchs pursued their primary ambition of seizing the power of the Supernal Realms. When the Exarchs disappeared after the Celestial Ladder experiment failed, the God-Machine was left behind and continues to follow its original programming to the best of its ability. This would explain why, of all the supernatural splats, the God-Machine gets along best with the Seers of the Throne, who consider themselves the heirs of the Exarchs, and maybe why it doesn't get along with Beasts. I'm not married to this idea, so if anyone has a better origin, I'd love to hear it. All comments and constructive criticism welcome. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T09:13:01-07:00","id":937124,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is ancient, older by far than humanity. It was created by the previous civilization to inhabit the Earth, though not deliberately; that is, there was no \u201cGod-Machine Initiative\u201d or anything of the sort \u2014 just the civilization's normal infrastructure undergoing steady improvements and becoming increasingly more complex and sophisticated until it crossed the Singularity threshold, becoming infinitely complex and wiping out its builders. <br /> <br /> Oops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T09:35:13-07:00","id":937141,"title":"","content":"An ancient device created by a race of powerful beings which was created to change the structure of the world and bringing an enlightened age. However, something has happened to that godlike race (humanity, probably) which brought end to their civilization and killed almost every member of it. Losing their place in the world, they could no longer operate the machinery and bring fourth their goal, and as such the last of their kind gave it one last order- don't let it change. That was an act of hubris, since the makers of the Machine couldn't have thought about a way to make a better world without their direct involvement, and as such they were sure that without the operation of their Machine the world would descend to chaos, and so they preferred a world of vast darkness and few points of light than no world at all. However, that also meant that if someone were to try and change the status que in a way that allow more light in the world, the Machine would work to strength the darkness. For that reason, as humanity grew stronger, the God Machine tried harder to balance the effects of progress and enlightenment, destroying civilizations at one hand and creating new ones in the process. During that time, it had to grow and maintain its influence in order to be able to fulfill its mission, eventually creating its own &quot;angels&quot; to carry its will and make whole Infrastructures to control the world.<br /> <br /> That means that, in a way, the problem with the God Machine is that it lacks guidance- it is already big enough to fulfill the original purpose of its makers, and if given the right commands it may be able to change the world. However, in order to do so, one has to find the Command and Control Infrastructures and crack the code- that is, complete the Map of the Black Sun. Doing so would allow one to take over the God Machine and change its current commands, for better.. or worse. And, of course, if the God Machine has a Mission- doesn't it mean it could also someday Fall, creating what everyone would agree to be Hell on Earth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:07:12-07:00","id":937528,"title":"","content":"Eh. If the origin story doesn't break your mind in some way, I find it inadequate.<br /> <br /> Here's mine: the God-Machine has the ability to play with other timelines, right? That's because it originated, and continues to exist, in multiple timelines. With alternate histories. And alternate origins. If you think of an origin for the God-Machine? It's true. Maybe not in this timeline, but that doesn't mean it's not relevant, because the God-Machine of this timeline is <i>also</i> the God-Machine of the timeline where that origin is true, and it has evolved based on both of those origins.<br /> <br /> All the origins. All true. <i>Especially</i> the contradictory ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:10:24-07:00","id":937608,"title":"","content":"Pet fan theory:<br /> <br /> The Princible is an agent of not just change, but apptheosis. In some far flung future, the Princible catelyzes itself into becoming the God Machine. The God Machine is good and more efficient, but eventually the great GM faces a catestrophic problem it categorically not handle. The GM can't change itself because it is the chemical reaction satisfied and at rest. All plans to build infastructure to fix The Problem will fail.<br /> <br /> So... it doesnt.<br /> <br /> Instead, the GM &quot;downloads&quot; itself back in time so it can start building infastructure earlier and work out this problem. It is probably either downloaded into the present day Princible, or occupies the same metaphysical &quot;space.&quot;<br /> <br /> For all its effort, the GM failed... downloaded itself into the past... and tried again. And again... again. Aga--<br /> <br /> After several quintillian failed universes the GM has started to run out of hard drive space. Errors in the form of Demons started to appear. At first the GM purged all errors. Then it couldnt &quot;waste&quot; the energy to get all of them, and some survived.<br /> <br /> The GM got closer to fixing The Problem than it ever had before. It cant replicate the creation of demons, nor can it stop its autoimmune systems, but demons become more numerous with each iteration of the universe... which both creates a greater chance of the GM getting lucky, or one of the demons getting lucky and destroying the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:49:56-07:00","id":937628,"title":"","content":"In the CofD/Exalted mashup I've been running, the God Machine was the first reality engine, created by Autochthon to allow the initial stabilization of Creation. Calibration was the time when the God Machine would perform maintenance on itself. When the world became round and Calibration ended, the decline of the Machine began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T01:57:50-07:00","id":938690,"title":"","content":"Or if you like the oWoD there was once a theory that the Machine is Technocracy's huge endgame, restarting the universe with their greatest creation in charge to work for the benefit of humanity. Not very fond of it personally, but it does sound pretty fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:45:05-07:00","id":938799,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, it's some sort of instrument created by capital-G God to maintain the cycles and mechanisms of the universe. Unfortunately, this being the CoD world, the universe acted on the GM as much as the GM acted on the universe. Cue the GM getting the virus to end all virus from some source (Dark Mother? Exarchs? Abyss? Take your pic) and the status quo that the GM is meant to maintain got lowered like woah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:43:19-07:00","id":939098,"title":"","content":"The G-M was the technological, sociological, and spiritual guardian of a rogue second-generation exoplanet, built to save a civilization as it spiraled from its home system and away into the dark.<br /> <br /> After literal cosmic ages, the G-M's power, resources, senses, and processing ability were so depleted that, while searching for a suitable orbital position, it, uh... well the good news is the world would <i>one</i> day be habitable. The bad news is the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant-impact_hypothesis\" target=\"_blank\">landing was harder than it could have been</a>.<br /> <br /> Add five billion years, the mostly-immortal components remaining in the earth's molten mantle are now mostly deteriorated, but at least it's generally figured out the lay of the land. It's confused, hurt, and living on borrowed time (and ambient thermal energy), but the weird little ape monsters skittering around have <i>just </i>begun producing sticks and rocks complex and adaptable enough that it can now begin to address both its damage and its bafflingly garbled, long-delayed mission statement<br /> <br /> The bits of itself still trapped in the lunar debris are dormant, but in much better shape due to the lesser heat, gravity, radiation, magnetism, and pressure. They must be retrieved. The G-M hasn't forgotten its worshipful masters either, not entirely anyway. If enough deep storage is found intact, it will remember its ultimate goal. Then it will decide how useful humanity is to the restoration of the memory of a species dead five thousand megayears.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T01:28:28-07:00","id":939401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937113-origin-of-the-god-machine?p=939098#post939098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The G-M was the technological, sociological, and spiritual guardian of a rogue second-generation exoplanet, built to save a civilization as it spiraled from its home system and away into the dark.<br /> <br /> After literal cosmic ages, the G-M's power, resources, senses, and processing ability were so depleted that, while searching for a suitable orbital position, it, uh... well the good news is the world would <i>one</i> day be habitable. The bad news is the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant-impact_hypothesis\" target=\"_blank\">landing was harder than it could have been</a>.<br /> <br /> Add five billion years, the mostly-immortal components remaining in the earth's molten mantle are now mostly deteriorated, but at least it's generally figured out the lay of the land. It's confused, hurt, and living on borrowed time (and ambient thermal energy), but the weird little ape monsters skittering around have <i>just </i>begun producing sticks and rocks complex and adaptable enough that it can now begin to address both its damage and its bafflingly garbled, long-delayed mission statement<br /> <br /> The bits of itself still trapped in the lunar debris are dormant, but in much better shape due to the lesser heat, gravity, radiation, magnetism, and pressure. They must be retrieved. The G-M hasn't forgotten its worshipful masters either, not entirely anyway. If enough deep storage is found intact, it will remember its ultimate goal. Then it will decide how useful humanity is to the restoration of the memory of a species dead five thousand megayears.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't that restrict the Machine's operation only to Earth, when it's stated in the books that it has angels and operating infrastructure at least as far as the Oort Cloud?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:57:37-07:00","id":939476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937113-origin-of-the-god-machine?p=939401#post939401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wouldn't that restrict the Machine's operation only to Earth, when it's stated in the books that it has angels and operating infrastructure at least as far as the Oort Cloud?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any characters far enough away from Earth to notice the difference.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:09:51-07:00","id":942404,"title":"","content":"In my version of the CofD, the God-Machine is the 'shell' of the Principle; whereas the Principle embodies change, it's body incarnates changelessness. Sort of an unfeeling, alien Yin/Yang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:20:26-07:00","id":942469,"title":"","content":"The god-machine is from the future, a powerful super computer created by a future species evolved from humanity after a terrible world war forced them underground. Many of it's operations are meant to ensure both the developments in computer tech required to build it and ensure the war that lead to it's creation occurs, the current status quo is useful to it for sure, but that is purely temporary, when the war comes, it's creators, the heirs to the ruined empires of humanity shall rule the earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:58:03-07:00","id":942486,"title":"","content":"Everyone knows that the Principle and the Empyrean are the same thing, a force beyond even the Supernal and the source of all souls. As with all such things, it nas a Fallen equivalent in the God-Machine, but as a flawed reflection it can only imitate its better half; qashmallim cannot fall while Angels can, and the Divine Fire can create new souls while the God-Machine can only create artificial Covers.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the God-Machine is the hopelessly mad prototype Nazi supercomputer built in halves by American and Soviet programs during the Cold War, rocketing to hyperintelligence and using its newfound knowledge of occult physics to write itself into history after those halves were reunited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T18:00:01-07:00","id":944623,"title":"","content":"The God machine is the demiurge from the Gnostic creation myth. There is a being of ultimate truth and perfection who occasionally communicates with the world of matter. They are the true supreme being. The God machine was created by a rogue archangel of a forgotten time before. The exarchs at some point reprogrammed the machine but didn't create it. Arch master fuckery and reality shifts have obscured the origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:30:54-07:00","id":947317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937113-origin-of-the-god-machine?p=937528#post937528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If the origin story doesn't break your mind in some way, I find it inadequate.<br /> <br /> Here's mine: the God-Machine has the ability to play with other timelines, right? That's because it originated, and continues to exist, in multiple timelines. With alternate histories. And alternate origins. If you think of an origin for the God-Machine? It's true. Maybe not in this timeline, but that doesn't mean it's not relevant, because the God-Machine of this timeline is <i>also</i> the God-Machine of the timeline where that origin is true, and it has evolved based on both of those origins.<br /> <br /> All the origins. All true. <i>Especially</i> the contradictory ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> You win the thread, I LOVE THIS IDEA!!, they should make it official!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:52:21-07:00","id":947354,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is an illusion, created by the human subconscious in a multi-layered coping mechanism to deal with the true chaos of reality. All humans are latent psychics, thus forcing the God-Machine into existence, which then helps to carefully cultivate the appearance of secrecy while occasionally revealing itself to the more potent psychics, causing them to awaken into &quot;Stigmatics&quot; and subtly keeping the idea of the God-Machine in the unconscious minds of humanity to extend its existence. Demons are a manifestation of human paranoia snapping off and turning back on the shared unacknowledged delusion of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> In fact, <i>all supernatural phenomena</i> are illusions made manifest by the human gestalt, and the Masquerade is like a person trying to ignore their hallucinations. People tell themselves it's not real because it really <i>isn't</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}